@@@!atrep

@@/ bibliogramma: a BibTeX-isomorphic bibliography format as an
@@/ atrep dialektos - an extension litogramma documents use for
@@/ references (englossis embedding; the cite mono links by
@@/ key). The data model is biblatex-shaped and covers the full
@@/ regular census of entry types and data fields; classic
@@/ BibTeX is the lossy export. Canonical terms are LATIN - the
@@/ entry genos draws from the genera vocabulary and the field
@@/ lemma from the campi vocabulary, with aliases across ~40
@@/ languages for the naturally-translatable terms (technical
@@/ terms carry Latin plus the biblatex name): a bibliography
@@/ authored in any covered language kanonizes, and hashes,
@@/ identically. Vocabulary-bound genoses are semantic and
@@/ survive litosis. Out of scope (Tier C, pass-through
@@/ verbatim): the relational machinery - crossref, xdata
@@/ inheritance, related, entryset - and processing hints
@@/ (options, sort*, short* names, ids); biber resolves those
@@/ downstream when the target is biblatex.

@=== entry
@& lemma
grammata
&@
@% genera
@"bibliography entry; lemma is the citation key, genos the genus"@
===@

@=== field
@: lemma=campi
grammata
:@
@"entry field; the lemma is the field name (campus)"@
===@

